    <h2>Re-Muxing vs Re-Encoding: Why Bitstream Copying Preserves 100% Video Quality</h2>
    <p>
      Many creators attempt to remove AI tags by importing clips into video editing software like Adobe Premiere, DaVinci Resolve, or HandBrake and re-exporting. However, this approach causes two serious issues:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Generational Compression Softening:</strong> Re-encoding an already compressed H.264 or HEVC stream applies a second layer of lossy macroblock quantization, blurring skin details, fine dust particles, and motion textures.</li>
      <li><strong>Extreme Processing Times:</strong> Re-encoding a 4K video clip requires minutes of heavy GPU rendering and drains laptop batteries.</li>
      <li><strong>The RemoveSynth Stream Advantage:</strong> Our tool performs bitstream demuxing and re-muxing (equivalent to <code>ffmpeg -c copy</code>). Because video frame bytes are copied directly without decompressing, processing takes less than 50 milliseconds and visual fidelity remains mathematically infinite ($PSNR = \infty$).</li>
    </ul>

